hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15832","al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, he said: Aqil ibn Abi Talib married, and he came out to us, so we said: With harmony and sons. He said: Hush, do not say that, for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us from that, and he said: Say: May Allah bless you and bless upon you and bless you in her."
"15833","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, that Aqil ibn Abi Talib married a woman from Banu Jusham, and the people came to him and said: With harmony and sons. He said: Do not say that. They said: What shall we say, O Abu Yazid? He said: Say: May Allah bless you and bless upon you; thus we were commanded."
